# Implementation Plan: Store-Wide Gallery Rollout

The user wants to deploy the fully tested, zoomed photo-gallery functionality from the Pokémon integration out to **all** product lines currently missing it.

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Model Updates (Admin Backend)
The current gallery upload system natively assumes any passed `card_id` belongs to the Pokémon database `cards`.
- **[MODIFY] `Admin_model.php`**: Upgrade `get_raw_card()` into a universal parser (`get_universal_card($id, $category)`). This will dynamically scan `mtg_cards`, `lorcana_cards`, `onepiece_cards`, or `custom_products` using its respective primary keys depending on the category passed, ensuring the Admin "Edit Photos" screen works and displays the correct item title.

### 2. Admin Controller Updates
- **[MODIFY] `Admin.php`**: Reconfigure the `edit_images()` and `upload_images_action()` functions to explicitly accept and forward the `$category` identifier alongside the `$card_id`.

### 3. Inventory UI Unlocks
We need to add the "📷 Photos" launch button to the admin tables!
- **[MODIFY] `admin/mtg_inventory.php`**, **`lorcana_inventory.php`**, **`onepiece_inventory.php`**, and **`custom_inventory.php`**: Inject the `href="<?= site_url('Admin/edit_images/' . card.id . '/mtg') ?>"` action buttons into the JavaScript table rendering logic.

### 4. Storefront Logic Injection
Fetch the uploaded photos and inject the Amazon-layout to the storefront pages!
- **[MODIFY] `Store.php`**: Hook `$this->Admin_model->get_card_images($id)` into the individual viewing controllers (`view_mtg_card`, `view_lorcana_card`, `view_onepiece_card`, `view_custom_product`).
- **[MODIFY] `view_mtg_card.php`, `view_lorcana_card.php`, `view_onepiece_card.php`, `view_custom_product.php`**: Implement the locked `500px` height wrapper, the `overflow: hidden` bounding box, the thumbnail mapping logic, and the perfectly smooth `.getBoundingClientRect` coordinate javascript magnifier tool we just refined for Pokémon.

---

> [!CAUTION]
> The only minor limitation: the gallery feature currently assumes independent card IDs. So long as a Custom Keychain does not accidentally use the exact same ID as a Lorcana ID (e.g. `TFC-001`), the photos will remain separate. This is extremely unlikely to ever happen since TCG sets use wildly different unique alphanumeric ID structures.

Let me know if this implementation plan is approved and I will rapidly execute it block by block!
